                        ],
                        "form": "die Kelten"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f64a8c87-c138-3172-93c8-3eddbe0d9adc",
                        "entry_id": "00389d99-4251-3587-953e-294e0d2bd55b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Angehöriger des Volks der Kelten"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9bacdf44-8fbd-4a33-9135-156b37efda79",
                                "sense_id": "f64a8c87-c138-3172-93c8-3eddbe0d9adc",
                                "text": "„Keltische Kriegerscharen fielen, von Gallien kommend, in Italien ein, die Römer stellten sich ihnen in der Schlacht an der Allia und erlitten eine katastrophale Niederlage. Sie hatten den Kelten nun nichts mehr entgegenzusetzen und mußten die Einnahme und Plünderung ihrer Stadt hinnehmen.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "84f064a9-1d62-4e3b-8708-82f487baef71",
                                "sense_id": "f64a8c87-c138-3172-93c8-3eddbe0d9adc",
                                "text": "„Für die ethnische Identität der Kelten war die Zugehörigkeit zu einem Stamm entscheidend.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6ff8f5b-e88f-4b43-aeab-968d08877ec1",
                                "sense_id": "f64a8c87-c138-3172-93c8-3eddbe0d9adc",
                                "text": "„Noch drei Jahrzehnte müssen vergehen, bis der römische Feldherr Gaius Julius Caesar die rechtsrheinischen Völker endlich zum ersten Mal »Germanen« nennt und klar von den linksrheinischen Kelten unterscheidet.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c72dc44b-bfc6-4770-bd9c-ab01359a9a9c",
                                "sense_id": "f64a8c87-c138-3172-93c8-3eddbe0d9adc",
                                "text": "„Schließlich sind keltische Kultplätze bloß die Orte, an denen Kelten in der Vergangenheit zu ihren Göttern gebetet und ihnen Opfer dargebracht haben.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fef18091-f06b-46ed-b2bb-7e7844e8dfdf",
                        "source_entry_id": "00389d99-4251-3587-953e-294e0d2bd55b",
                        "source_sense_id": "f64a8c87-c138-3172-93c8-3eddbe0d9adc",
                        "source_sense_description": "Angehöriger des Volks der Kelten",
                        "target_lang_word": "Celt",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Celt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9bf37c79-9b57-3ad0-a2bb-76e3f88f77dd",
                                        "entry_id": "8a7e2222-5e5a-338c-9283-910d7c2fd604",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of one of the ancient peoples of Western Europe called Celtae by the Romans."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d41d67c-c4b5-34dd-b0f6-b1a840be15a9",
                                        "entry_id": "8a7e2222-5e5a-338c-9283-910d7c2fd604",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of any of the (modern, Celtic) peoples who speak Celtic languages."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Celt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "576d124d-2a98-3f74-8b20-d19d227b84bf",
                                        "entry_id": "6dc5c5cc-d029-36c3-b5ee-7688e6916662",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of Celtic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0dbaf09-1bcb-4c19-9a3a-a32d743a4cc7",
                                                "sense_id": "576d124d-2a98-3f74-8b20-d19d227b84bf",
                                                "text": "In the thick of parties we become very Celt, disgusting the dull."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b4052ba-f3c8-40a7-ba18-133a1333556e",
                                                "sense_id": "576d124d-2a98-3f74-8b20-d19d227b84bf",
                                                "text": "Like Pris, he took after their mother, more Celt than English, wild and dramatic and mercurially alive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d76a8725-4f1b-43e9-bdb4-03f64701a38d",
                                                "sense_id": "576d124d-2a98-3f74-8b20-d19d227b84bf",
                                                "text": "But his bitch queen was Saxon to the bone and her legacy showed in the sons that Vortigern bred off her. Katigern Minor might be young, but he has become what his grandfather never was – more Saxon than Celt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "396d0744-cf69-41b0-a0c0-251107c92ba9",
                                                "sense_id": "576d124d-2a98-3f74-8b20-d19d227b84bf",
                                                "text": "She answered with a smile and a nod. The woman was more Celt than Arienh had thought, and had clearly been deprived of women too long."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b49f6225-37af-441f-b014-94af320af3a3",
                        "source_entry_id": "00389d99-4251-3587-953e-294e0d2bd55b",
                        "source_sense_id": "f64a8c87-c138-3172-93c8-3eddbe0d9adc",
                        "source_sense_description": "Angehöriger des Volks der Kelten",
                        "target_lang_word": "Kelt",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kelt",
